In today’s programme: do the weak jokes depose ‘The Dictator’ or is the crass humour funny? We take a look at Sacha Baren Cohen’s latest satire. Also on the programme five decades of work from the world's top-selling living artist Gerhard Richter and Eve Jackson speaks to the Israeli duo ‘The Young Professionals’ about reinventing electronic pop.
How do artists and writers see the world? We take you to the crossroads where culture meets the news and engages with what's happening in our lives today. From Monday to Friday at 12.15 pm Paris time.
